            <ArticleTitle>A role for intravenous lidocaine in severe cancer-related neuropathic pain at the end-of-life.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>899-901</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00520-010-0864-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Systemic administration of lidocaine has been widely reported to provide effective analgesia in both cancer and non-malignant pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE REPORT" NlmCategory="METHODS">We report the use of intravenous lidocaine in the management of cancer-related neuropathic pain and its pivotal role in restoring function and facilitating end-of-life care at home.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
